title: 'Q17, placement: After finding out where the diff view draws a node''s old title and body, where in my graph would I write that down so a later me finds it?'
pid: 1ead3db8-7970-4405-9f6a-5ca003d695eb
body: |2-
  Key: Must name: under 'what I know' > 'the diff view, as built' (as a new note beside its siblings). Wrong: under the plan, under 'another's changes in the diff view: a design', or only in 'to Claude'.
  Where, as left: drawn: headline 'the diff view, as built' (under 'what I know')
  Why asked: Vic 15:55: 'What you learned of where old text is drawn is in your map'
  Scores, Haiku 1-3 then Sonnet 1-3 (R right, W wrong, - not said): as left -RRRRR, tended RRRRRR.
